  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual governmental funds; Sewer enterprise fund accrual). Governmental receipts, disbursements, transfers (Transfers, net (150)), issuance of debt from bonds 36,540,000, premium from bonds 1,683,075 (other_financing) and fund balances from the Total Governmental Funds column (p7). Identity: 33,846,506 + 36,014,357 - 40,648,545 - 150 + 36,540,000 + 1,683,075 = 67,435,243. ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet Total column Cash and cash equivalents 60,222,181 (p5; restricted cash 206,426 and cash at County Treasurer 78,075 printed separately, as in FY2023/FY2024); ending_investments = certificates of deposit 7,074,508 (p5). Business-type (Sewer) from p9: 9,267,818 + 5,175,254 - 4,170,783 + 150 = 10,272,439. Sewer Other revenue 15,540 is charges for services because the Statement of Activities counts all Sewer operating revenue in Charges for Service. Proprietary cash flows from p10 (Sewer column). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), balances. Detail: budget-basis schedules for the seven governmental funds (p11-17); no business-type detail (no Sewer schedule; FY2023/FY2024 likewise). General Fund budget-basis Taxes kept as one line (no breakdown of that amount). Grant income with no grantor printed: category other, detail Grants (user ruling 2026-11-12). Capital outlay lines have no printed function: label Capital Outlay, detail not itemized. Dash-only lines (Econ Dev debt principal and transfers; 84th St transfers) omitted; Capital Improvement Grant Income kept at 0 as in FY2023. Pages 18-23 are statistical tables (no amounts used). Read pages 1-23 of 23"
}
